  "airline": "ASA",
  "name": "Xáat Kwáani (\"Salmon People\")",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "B738",
  "description": "Fuselage: Whole fuselage in blues: dark midnight blue base with lighter Atlas blue areas (Alaska named the palette Midnight Blue, Atlas Blue, White and Pink). Cheatlines: None; instead a single stylized white salmon in Northwest Coast formline style runs the full length of the fuselage. Tail: A second formline salmon dives down the fin (replaces the usual Alaska Native man). Engines: Atlas-blue cowlings, midnight blue low down. Winglets: Repeat the stylized salmon from the tail. Titles: A white 'Alaska' title over the wing root on Atlas blue, riding over the window line, about half the standard size; 'Xáat Kwáani / SALMON PEOPLE' small in pink on the nose. Artwork: Formline salmon by Tlingit/Athabascan artist Crystal Kaakeeyáa Worl; pink splashes accent the salmon; 'Xáat Kwáani' means Salmon People in Tlingit. Colors hex: not published; colors approximate.",
